{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Forty years.</b> But are not thirty days missing? For on the fifteenth of Iyar the manna first fell for them, and on the fifteenth of Nisan it ceased, as is said: ״וַיִּשְׁבֹּת הַמָּן מִמָּחֳרָת״ (Joshua 5)? Rather, it tells that the cakes which Israel brought out of Egypt tasted to them like the taste of manna (Kiddushin 38)." "<b>Unto a settled land.</b> After they crossed the Jordan — for that one across the Jordan is settled and good, as is said: ״אֶעְבְּרָה נָּא וְאֶרְאֶה אֶת הָאָרֶץ הַטּוֹבָה אֲשֶׁר בְּעֵבֶר הַיַּרְדֵּן״, and the Targum of נוֹשָׁבֶת is יָתְבָתָא — that is to say, settled." "<b>Unto the border of the land of Canaan.</b> At the beginning of the border, before they crossed the Jordan — and that is the plains of Moab. Do they then contradict one another? Rather, in the plains of Moab, when Moses died on the seventh of Adar, the manna ceased to fall, and they supplied themselves from manna they had gathered on that day until they brought the omer on the sixteenth of Nisan, as is said: ״וַיֹּאכְלוּ מֵעֲבוּר הָאָרֶץ מִמָּחֳרַת הַפֶּסַח״ (Joshua 5)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:50.194664544Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}